#: manual/tutorial/core.md:1
msgid "core tutorial"
msgstr "core 教程"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:3
msgid "This tutorial shows how to create variable names, generate fresh ones, keep track of the names in scope and rename variables with the `core` package. By the end you can give your own syntax a name type that the rest of `type_theory` understands."
msgstr "本教程展示如何使用 `core` 包创建变量名、生成新鲜名字、跟踪作用域中的名字以及重命名变量。学完之后，你就能为自己的语法提供一种 `type_theory` 其余部分都能理解的名字类型。"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:10
msgid "make a variable name"
msgstr "构造变量名"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:11
msgid "pick a name that clashes with nothing in use"
msgstr "选取一个与所有已用名字都不冲突的名字"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:12
msgid "record the names in scope"
msgstr "记录作用域内的名字"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:13
msgid "record binders with annotations in order"
msgstr "按顺序记录带标注的绑定子"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:14
msgid "rename several variables at once"
msgstr "同时重命名多个变量"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:18
msgid "Add the module and import the package:"
msgstr "添加该模块并导入包："

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:31
msgid "The smallest useful program picks a name that does not clash with the names already in use:"
msgstr "最小的实用程序会选取一个不与已用名字冲突的名字："

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:42
msgid "`fresh_name` keeps the hint `x` when it is unused and otherwise appends the smallest suffix `_1`, `_2`, … that is not taken."
msgstr "`fresh_name` 在提示名 `x` 未被使用时保留它，否则追加未被占用的最小后缀 `_1`、`_2`、…。"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:47
msgid "Name the parameters of a generated function"
msgstr "为生成的函数命名参数"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:49
msgid "When a program generates code, it often needs several parameter names that avoid each other and the names already in the surrounding code. Add each new name to the used set before choosing the next:"
msgstr "程序生成代码时，常常需要若干个参数名，它们彼此不冲突，也不与周围代码中已有的名字冲突。在选择下一个名字之前，先把每个新名字加入已用集合："

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:66
msgid "The result depends only on the hint and the used set, so the same input always produces the same names."
msgstr "结果只取决于提示名和已用集合，因此相同的输入总是产生相同的名字。"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:69
msgid "Track the names in scope"
msgstr "跟踪作用域中的名字"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:71
msgid "A `Context` records binders from the outside in. A later binder with the same name shadows an earlier one, and the context keeps both:"
msgstr "`Context` 从外到内记录绑定子。同名的较晚绑定子会遮蔽较早的，而上下文会同时保留两者："

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:87
msgid "`extend_with` returns a new context and leaves `outer` unchanged, so you can keep the context of each level of a traversal without copying it yourself."
msgstr "`extend_with` 返回新的上下文并保持 `outer` 不变，因此你可以保留遍历中每一层的上下文，而无需自己复制。"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:90
msgid "Rename variables"
msgstr "重命名变量"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:92
msgid "A `Renaming` maps some names to others and leaves every other name alone. All entries apply at once:"
msgstr "`Renaming` 将某些名字映射为其他名字，其余名字保持不变。所有条目同时生效："

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:106
msgid "Because the renaming is simultaneous, swapping needs no temporary name."
msgstr "由于重命名是同时进行的，交换两个名字不需要临时名字。"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:108
msgid "Compose renamings and respect binders"
msgstr "复合重命名并尊重绑定子"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:110
msgid "`r.then(s)` applies `r` and then `s`. Under a binder for `x`, remove `x` from the renaming with `without`, because the bound `x` is a different variable:"
msgstr "`r.then(s)` 先应用 `r` 再应用 `s`。在 `x` 的绑定子之下，要用 `without` 从重命名中去掉 `x`，因为被绑定的 `x` 是另一个变量："

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:126
msgid "Describe a parameter list with a telescope"
msgstr "用伸缩式描述参数列表"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:128
msgid "A `Telescope` stores binders with annotations, in the order in which later annotations may refer to earlier binders:"
msgstr "`Telescope` 存储带注解的绑定子，其顺序保证后面的注解可以引用前面的绑定子："

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:145
msgid "Bridge your own variable type"
msgstr "桥接你自己的变量类型"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:147
msgid "A downstream library usually has its own variable type, for example a variable with an index. Give it a conversion to `Name` so that it can use the binding algorithms of `type_theory`:"
msgstr "下游库通常有自己的变量类型，例如带索引的变量。为它提供到 `Name` 的转换，使其能够使用 `type_theory` 的绑定算法："

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:166
msgid "The conversion must be injective on the variables you use: two different variables must not map to the same name."
msgstr "该转换在你使用的变量上必须是单射：两个不同的变量不能映射到同一个名字。"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:169
msgid "Avoid all names, not only free ones"
msgstr "避开所有名字，而不仅是自由名字"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:171
msgid "`fresh_name` only knows the set you give it. When you rename a binder, put every name of the term into that set (free, bound and binder names), plus the names of anything you are about to insert. The [syntax](../api/syntax.md) helpers `all_names` and `generic_all_names` compute this set."
msgstr "`fresh_name` 只知道你给它的集合。重命名绑定子时，要把项中的每个名字（自由名字、约束名字和绑定子名字）以及你即将插入的任何东西中的名字都放进这个集合。[syntax](../api/syntax.md) 中的辅助函数 `all_names` 和 `generic_all_names` 可以计算这个集合。"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:178
msgid "**Comparing renamings.** `==` on `Renaming` compares entry lists. Two renamings that act the same, such as `empty()` and `singleton(x, x)`, are not `==`. Compare their action on the names you care about instead."
msgstr "**比较重命名。** `Renaming` 上的 `==` 比较的是条目列表。两个行为相同的重命名（例如 `empty()` 和 `singleton(x, x)`）并不 `==`。请改为比较它们在你关心的名字上的作用。"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:181
msgid "**Mutating a context.** There is nothing to mutate: `extend_with` returns a new value. Forgetting to use the result is the usual mistake."
msgstr "**修改上下文。** 没有什么可修改的：`extend_with` 返回一个新值。忘记使用返回结果是常见错误。"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:183
msgid "**Old method names.** `Context::extend`, `Telescope::extend` and the `extend` forms in `stlc` are deprecated aliases; use `extend_with`."
msgstr "**旧的方法名。** `Context::extend`、`Telescope::extend` 以及 `stlc` 中的 `extend` 形式都是已弃用的别名；请使用 `extend_with`。"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:185
msgid "**Long contexts.** Every `extend_with` copies the array. Building a context of $n$ names one by one costs $O(n^2)$; use `Context::from_array` when you have all names at once."
msgstr "**过长的上下文。** 每次 `extend_with` 都会复制数组。逐个添加来构建含 $n$ 个名字的上下文的代价是 $O(n^2)$；如果一次就有全部名字，请使用 `Context::from_array`。"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:191
msgid "The [core API](../api/core.md) lists every function with its exact signature."
msgstr "[core API](../api/core.md) 列出了每个函数及其确切签名。"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:193
msgid "The [core design](../design/core.md) proves the freshness and composition laws used here."
msgstr "[core 设计](../design/core.md)证明了这里用到的新鲜性定律和复合定律。"

#: manual/tutorial/core.md:195
msgid "The [syntax tutorial](syntax.md) uses names to build terms with binders."
msgstr "[syntax 教程](syntax.md)使用名字构建带绑定子的项。"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:1
msgid "debruijn tutorial"
msgstr "debruijn 教程"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:3
msgid "This tutorial converts named lambda terms to De Bruijn form, uses that form to compare terms and to reduce them without renaming, validates untrusted nameless input, and converts results back to names for display."
msgstr "本教程将命名 lambda 项转换为 De Bruijn 形式，利用这种形式比较项并在无需重命名的情况下归约它们，验证不可信的无名输入，并将结果转换回带名字的形式以便显示。"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:9
msgid "convert a named term to indices"
msgstr "把具名项转换为索引"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:10
msgid "convert back with readable names"
msgstr "转换回带可读名字的项"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:11
msgid "check that every index has a binder"
msgstr "检查每个索引都有对应的绑定子"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:12
msgid "reduce without renaming"
msgstr "不重命名地归约"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:13
msgid "open a binder with an argument"
msgstr "用一个实参打开绑定子"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:14
msgid "move a term under binders"
msgstr "把项移到绑定子之下"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:31
msgid "$\\lambda x.\\,\\lambda y.\\,x$ becomes $\\lambda.\\,\\lambda.\\,1$: the variable refers to the binder one level further out."
msgstr "$\\lambda x.\\,\\lambda y.\\,x$ 变为 $\\lambda.\\,\\lambda.\\,1$：该变量指向向外一层的绑定子。"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:45
#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:96
msgid "Compare terms up to bound names"
msgstr "在约束名字的意义下比较项"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:47
msgid "Alpha-equivalent named terms have equal De Bruijn forms, so `==` after conversion decides alpha-equivalence:"
msgstr "α-等价的命名项具有相同的 De Bruijn 形式，因此转换后的 `==` 可判定 α-等价："

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:58
msgid "`@syntax.alpha_equal` gives the same answer without building the converted terms; the conversion pays off when you keep the nameless form for further work."
msgstr "`@syntax.alpha_equal` 无需构建转换后的项即可给出相同的答案；当你需要保留无名形式做进一步处理时，转换才物有所值。"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:62
msgid "Reduce without renaming"
msgstr "无需重命名的归约"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:64
msgid "Beta reduction on nameless terms shifts indices instead of renaming binders. The classic capture example $(\\lambda x.\\,\\lambda y.\\,x)\\,y$ needs no fresh name:"
msgstr "在无名项上的 β-归约通过移位索引而不是重命名绑定子来完成。经典的捕获示例 $(\\lambda x.\\,\\lambda y.\\,x)\\,y$ 不需要新鲜名字："

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:79
msgid "The free `y` stays free because it is a name, and the inner binder needs no new name because it has none."
msgstr "自由的 `y` 保持自由，因为它是一个名字；内层绑定子不需要新名字，因为它根本没有名字。"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:82
msgid "Validate untrusted input"
msgstr "验证不可信的输入"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:84
msgid "Terms built by hand or read from outside can contain indices that point past every binder. Check them before reducing:"
msgstr "手工构建或从外部读取的项可能包含超出所有绑定子的索引。请在归约之前检查它们："

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:100
msgid "Convert back to names for display"
msgstr "转换回带名字的形式以便显示"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:102
msgid "`to_named` names binders `x`, `x_1`, … and avoids the free names of the term:"
msgstr "`to_named` 将绑定子命名为 `x`、`x_1`、…，并避开项中的自由名字："

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:118
msgid "The binders skip `x` because `x` is free in the term."
msgstr "绑定子跳过了 `x`，因为 `x` 在项中是自由的。"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:120
msgid "Open a binder by hand"
msgstr "手工打开绑定子"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:122
msgid "`instantiate(body, arg)` is the result of $(\\lambda.\\,body)\\,arg$. Use it when you implement your own reducer or evaluator:"
msgstr "`instantiate(body, arg)` 是 $(\\lambda.\\,body)\\,arg$ 的结果。在实现你自己的归约器或求值器时使用它："

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:138
msgid "Check the named reducer against the nameless one"
msgstr "用无名归约器检验命名归约器"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:140
msgid "Because the conversion commutes with beta reduction, the named and nameless reducers must agree up to alpha-equivalence. This is a good property test for any reducer you write:"
msgstr "由于转换与 β-归约可交换，命名归约器与无名归约器必须在 α-等价意义下一致。对于你编写的任何归约器，这都是一个很好的性质测试："

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:166
msgid "(This example also imports `Luna-Flow/type_theory/substitution`.)"
msgstr "（此示例还导入了 `Luna-Flow/type_theory/substitution`。）"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:168
msgid "Fast normalization"
msgstr "快速范式化"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:170
msgid "`normalize` repeats one search-and-contract step from the root, which is simple and traceable but slow on long reductions. For large untyped terms use [utlc/nbe](utlc/nbe.md), which works on the same `DbTerm` and returns the same normal forms (up to the shape of application spines)."
msgstr "`normalize` 从根部反复执行一次“搜索并收缩”的步骤，简单且可追踪，但对于很长的归约很慢。对于大型无类型项，请使用 [utlc/nbe](utlc/nbe.md)，它作用于相同的 `DbTerm` 并返回相同的范式（在应用脊的形状意义下）。"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:177
msgid "**Counting indices from the outside.** `Bound(0)` is the *innermost* binder. $\\lambda x.\\,\\lambda y.\\,x$ is `Bind(Bind(Bound(1)))`, not `Bound(0)`."
msgstr "**从外向内计数索引。** `Bound(0)` 是*最内层*的绑定子。$\\lambda x.\\,\\lambda y.\\,x$ 是 `Bind(Bind(Bound(1)))`，而不是 `Bound(0)`。"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:180
msgid "**Reducing unvalidated terms.** `reduce_once` and `substitute_bound` do not detect unbound indices. Call `validate` first on input you did not build with `from_named`."
msgstr "**归约未经验证的项。** `reduce_once` 和 `substitute_bound` 不会检测未绑定的索引。对于不是用 `from_named` 构建的输入，请先调用 `validate`。"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:183
msgid "**Expecting binder names to survive.** `to_named(from_named(t))` is alpha-equivalent to `t`, but binder names are regenerated."
msgstr "**期望绑定子名字得以保留。** `to_named(from_named(t))` 与 `t` α-等价，但绑定子名字是重新生成的。"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:185
msgid "**Spines.** `Apply(f, [a, b])` and `Apply(Apply(f, [a]), [b])` mean the same application but are different values; normalize them to one shape before comparing with `==`."
msgstr "**应用脊。** `Apply(f, [a, b])` 和 `Apply(Apply(f, [a]), [b])` 表示同一个应用，但它们是不同的值；用 `==` 比较之前请先将它们规整为同一种形状。"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:191
msgid "[debruijn API](../api/debruijn.md) for every function and error case."
msgstr "[debruijn API](../api/debruijn.md)：每个函数和错误情形。"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:192
msgid "[debruijn design](../design/debruijn.md) for shifting, instantiation and the correctness lemmas."
msgstr "[debruijn 设计](../design/debruijn.md)：移位、实例化以及正确性引理。"

#: manual/tutorial/debruijn.md:194
msgid "[utlc/nbe tutorial](utlc/nbe.md) for normalization by evaluation on `DbTerm`."
msgstr "[utlc/nbe 教程](utlc/nbe.md)：`DbTerm` 上的求值范式化。"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:1
msgid "eval tutorial"
msgstr "eval 教程"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:3
msgid "This tutorial runs a rewrite rule with the named strategies of `eval`: normal order, applicative order and weak head. You will see where they agree, where they differ, and how to write a strategy of your own. The examples use the beta rule of the untyped lambda calculus from `utlc/lambda`."
msgstr "本教程使用 `eval` 中的具名策略运行一条改写规则：正规序、应用序和弱头。你将看到它们在哪些地方一致、在哪些地方不同，以及如何编写你自己的策略。示例使用 `utlc/lambda` 中无类型 lambda 演算的 β 规则。"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:10
msgid "reduce to a normal form whenever one exists"
msgstr "只要存在范式就归约到范式"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:11
msgid "reduce arguments first"
msgstr "先归约参数"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:12
msgid "stop at weak head normal form"
msgstr "在弱头范式处停止"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:13
msgid "take a single step"
msgstr "执行单步"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:14
msgid "see every step"
msgstr "查看每一步"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:15
msgid "use a strategy that is not in the enum"
msgstr "使用枚举中没有的策略"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:15
msgid "a step function for `@rewrite.normalize`"
msgstr "用于 `@rewrite.normalize` 的步进函数"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:33
msgid "Apply the identity function to `42`:"
msgstr "将恒等函数应用于 `42`："

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:49
msgid "The tasks share these helpers:"
msgstr "各任务共用以下辅助函数："

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:67
msgid "Pick a strategy that terminates"
msgstr "选择一个会终止的策略"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:69
msgid "Normal order is normalizing: if a term has a normal form, it finds it. Applicative order evaluates arguments first and loops on a divergent argument even when it is thrown away:"
msgstr "正规序是范式化的：如果一个项有范式，它就能找到。应用序先对参数求值，即使某个发散的参数最终被丢弃，也会在其上陷入死循环："

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:87
msgid "Evaluate only to weak head normal form"
msgstr "只求值到弱头范式"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:89
msgid "`WeakHead` stops as soon as the term is an abstraction or an application with a non-reducible head. It does not look inside:"
msgstr "一旦项是抽象，或是头部不可归约的应用，`WeakHead` 就立即停止。它不会查看内部："

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:108
msgid "The result $\\lambda f.\\,(\\lambda x.\\,x)\\,f$ still contains a redex under the binder; `NormalOrder` would reduce it."
msgstr "结果 $\\lambda f.\\,(\\lambda x.\\,x)\\,f$ 在绑定子之下仍包含一个可约式；`NormalOrder` 会将其归约。"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:111
msgid "Trace the steps"
msgstr "追踪各个步骤"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:113
msgid "`trace` records each step with its path, which is useful to explain a normalization or to compare two strategies step by step:"
msgstr "`trace` 记录每一步及其路径，这对于解释一次范式化或逐步比较两种策略很有用："

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:134
msgid "Both steps happen at the root: first $K\\,1$ is contracted inside the spine $K\\,1\\,\\Omega$, then the result is applied to $\\Omega$, which is discarded."
msgstr "两步都发生在根部：先在脊 $K\\,1\\,\\Omega$ 内部收缩 $K\\,1$，然后将结果应用于 $\\Omega$，后者被丢弃。"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:137
msgid "Use a domain rule"
msgstr "使用领域规则"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:139
msgid "Strategies work with any rule, not only beta. Here a rule folds additions of literals; normal order folds the outer addition last:"
msgstr "策略适用于任何规则，而不仅是 β。这里有一条折叠字面量加法的规则；正规序最后才折叠外层的加法："

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:163
msgid "Write your own strategy"
msgstr "编写你自己的策略"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:165
msgid "Any function from a term to a `StepResult` is a strategy for `@rewrite.normalize`. This one reduces only at the root, which is useful to test a rule in isolation:"
msgstr "任何从项到 `StepResult` 的函数都是 `@rewrite.normalize` 的一种策略。下面这个只在根部归约，便于单独测试一条规则："

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:190
msgid "A hand-written step must keep the contract of `StepResult`: `after` is `before` with exactly the subterm at `path` rewritten."
msgstr "手写的步骤必须遵守 `StepResult` 的约定：`after` 恰好是将 `before` 在 `path` 处的子项改写后的结果。"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:193
msgid "Check strategies against each other"
msgstr "相互检验策略"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:195
msgid "For a confluent rule such as beta, two strategies that both reach a normal form agree up to alpha-equivalence. This makes a cheap regression test:"
msgstr "对于 β 这样具有合流性的规则，两个都到达范式的策略在 α-等价意义下一致。这构成了一种低成本的回归测试："

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:219
msgid "**Reading `WeakHead`'s `NormalForm` as a full normal form.** It only means weak head normal form."
msgstr "**把 `WeakHead` 的 `NormalForm` 当作完全范式。** 它只表示弱头范式。"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:221
msgid "**Expecting `FullNormal` to differ from `NormalOrder`.** Today they use the same traversal."
msgstr "**期望 `FullNormal` 与 `NormalOrder` 不同。** 目前它们使用相同的遍历。"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:223
msgid "**Comparing results with `==`.** Beta reduction renames binders (`y_1`); compare with `@syntax.alpha_equal`."
msgstr "**用 `==` 比较结果。** β-归约会重命名绑定子（`y_1`）；请用 `@syntax.alpha_equal` 比较。"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:225
msgid "**Too small a step limit.** `StepLimitReached` does not mean divergence. Raise the limit, or use [utlc/nbe](utlc/nbe.md) for fast untyped normalization."
msgstr "**步数上限太小。** `StepLimitReached` 并不意味着发散。请提高上限，或使用 [utlc/nbe](utlc/nbe.md) 进行快速的无类型范式化。"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:231
msgid "[eval API](../api/eval.md) for the exact signatures."
msgstr "[eval API](../api/eval.md)：确切的签名。"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:232
msgid "[eval design](../design/eval.md) for the definitions of the strategies and the classical theorems behind them."
msgstr "[eval 设计](../design/eval.md)：各策略的定义及其背后的经典定理。"

#: manual/tutorial/eval.md:234
msgid "[utlc/lambda tutorial](utlc/lambda.md) for the lambda calculus built on these strategies."
msgstr "[utlc/lambda 教程](utlc/lambda.md)：建立在这些策略之上的 lambda 演算。"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:1
msgid "rewrite tutorial"
msgstr "rewrite 教程"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:3
msgid "This tutorial writes simplification rules for arithmetic terms, applies them one step at a time, runs them to a normal form with a step limit, and reads the trace to see which rule fired where. Terms are `Term[String]` with operators as values: $x \\cdot 1$ is `Apply(Value(\"*\"), [Variable(x), Value(\"1\")])`."
msgstr "本教程为算术项编写化简规则，逐步应用它们，在步数上限内将它们运行到范式，并阅读追踪记录以了解哪条规则在何处触发。项的类型是 `Term[String]`，运算符作为值：$x \\cdot 1$ 是 `Apply(Value(\"*\"), [Variable(x), Value(\"1\")])`。"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:11
msgid "apply a rule once, outermost first"
msgstr "应用一次规则，最外层优先"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:12
msgid "apply a rule once, innermost first"
msgstr "应用一次规则，最内层优先"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:13
msgid "repeat steps with a limit"
msgstr "带上限地重复执行步骤"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:14
msgid "keep every step for inspection"
msgstr "保留每一步以供检查"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:15
msgid "name a rule"
msgstr "为规则命名"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:15
msgid "`RuleName::new` or, for literals, `RuleName::unsafe_new`"
msgstr "`RuleName::new`，或对于字面量使用 `RuleName::unsafe_new`"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:16
msgid "rewrite my own AST"
msgstr "重写我自己的 AST"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:32
msgid "A rule is a function that rewrites a term at its root or returns `None`. The rule $t \\cdot 1 \\to t$ simplifies $(x \\cdot 1) \\cdot 1$ in two steps:"
msgstr "规则是一个在项的根部改写该项或返回 `None` 的函数。规则 $t \\cdot 1 \\to t$ 用两步化简 $(x \\cdot 1) \\cdot 1$："

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:57
msgid "These examples share a few helpers and a second rule, $0 + t \\to t$:"
msgstr "这些示例共用几个辅助函数和第二条规则 $0 + t \\to t$："

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:80
msgid "Take one step and see where it happened"
msgstr "执行一步并查看发生的位置"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:82
msgid "`top_down_once` rewrites the outermost-leftmost match and reports the path to it:"
msgstr "`top_down_once` 改写最外最左的匹配，并报告到达它的路径："

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:100
msgid "`ApplyArgument(1)` is the second argument of the root `*`."
msgstr "`ApplyArgument(1)` 是根部 `*` 的第二个参数。"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:102
msgid "Normalize with a step limit"
msgstr "在步数上限内范式化"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:104
msgid "A step limit protects against rules that never stop. Check which result you got:"
msgstr "步数上限可以防止永不停止的规则。请检查你得到的是哪种结果："

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:123
msgid "Read a trace"
msgstr "阅读追踪记录"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:125
msgid "`trace` keeps every step, so you can explain a simplification:"
msgstr "`trace` 保留每一步，因此你可以解释一次化简过程："

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:143
msgid "Choose outermost or innermost"
msgstr "选择最外或最内"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:145
msgid "When redexes are nested, `top_down_once` takes the outer one and `bottom_up_once` the inner one. With a confluent rule set both reach the same normal form, but the steps differ:"
msgstr "当可约式嵌套时，`top_down_once` 选择外层的，`bottom_up_once` 选择内层的。对于具有合流性的规则集，两者到达相同的范式，但步骤不同："

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:165
msgid "Combine several rules"
msgstr "组合多条规则"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:167
msgid "Combine rules into one by trying them in order. The combined rule has one name; give it a name that says so:"
msgstr "通过按顺序尝试，将多条规则组合成一条。组合后的规则只有一个名字；请给它一个能说明这一点的名字："

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:186
msgid "If you need to know which of the rules fired, write a step function that calls `top_down_once` once per rule, each with its own name, and returns the first `Reduced`. That prefers the first rule anywhere in the term over the second rule at an outer position."
msgstr "如果需要知道是哪条规则触发了，请编写一个步进函数，对每条规则各调用一次 `top_down_once`（各自使用自己的名字），并返回第一个 `Reduced`。这样会优先选择项中任意位置的第一条规则，而不是更外层位置上的第二条规则。"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:193
msgid "Rules under binders"
msgstr "绑定子之下的规则"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:195
msgid "Traversals enter binder bodies, so a rule sees open terms. A rule that only looks at the shape of a term, like the two above, is fine anywhere. A rule that moves or duplicates subterms across binders must handle binding itself, usually with [substitution](substitution.md). The beta rule of [`@lambda`](utlc/lambda.md) is the standard example."
msgstr "遍历会进入绑定子的体，因此规则会看到开项。像上面两条那样只查看项的形状的规则，在任何位置都没有问题。跨越绑定子移动或复制子项的规则必须自己处理绑定，通常借助[代换](substitution.md)。[`@lambda`](utlc/lambda.md) 的 β 规则就是标准示例。"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:201
msgid "Rewriting your own AST"
msgstr "重写你自己的 AST"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:203
msgid "`generic_top_down_once` and `generic_normalize` accept any AST that implements `@syntax.BindingSyntax`. Write the rule against your own type; the [adapter tutorial](adapter.md) shows a complete example."
msgstr "`generic_top_down_once` 和 `generic_normalize` 接受任何实现了 `@syntax.BindingSyntax` 的 AST。针对你自己的类型编写规则即可；[adapter 教程](adapter.md)给出了完整示例。"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:209
msgid "[eval](eval.md) packages the traversals as named strategies (normal order, applicative order, weak head) behind one `evaluate` function."
msgstr "[eval](eval.md) 把这些遍历包装成具名策略（正规序、应用序、弱头），统一放在一个 `evaluate` 函数之后。"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:214
msgid "**A rule that does not make progress.** A rule that returns `Some(t)` for its own input $t$, or that undoes another rule, keeps the normalizer busy until the step limit. Check for `StepLimitReached`."
msgstr "**不推进的规则。** 对自身输入 $t$ 返回 `Some(t)` 的规则，或抵消另一条规则的规则，会让范式化器一直忙到步数上限。请检查 `StepLimitReached`。"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:217
msgid "**Non-confluent rules.** If two rules overlap without joining, different strategies can give different normal forms. Use the trace to find the overlap."
msgstr "**非合流的规则。** 如果两条规则重叠却不能汇合，不同策略可能给出不同的范式。用轨迹找出重叠之处。"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:220
msgid "**`unsafe_new` with input.** `RuleName::unsafe_new(\"\")` aborts. Use `RuleName::new` for names that are not literals."
msgstr "**对输入使用 `unsafe_new`。** `RuleName::unsafe_new(\"\")` 会中止程序。对非字面量的名使用 `RuleName::new`。"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:222
msgid "**Ambiguous constructors.** `@syntax.Variable(x)` without an expected type is ambiguous; write `@syntax.Term::Variable(x)`."
msgstr "**有歧义的构造子。** 没有期望类型时，`@syntax.Variable(x)` 有歧义；请写 `@syntax.Term::Variable(x)`。"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:227
msgid "[rewrite API](../api/rewrite.md) for every type and function."
msgstr "[rewrite API](../api/rewrite.md)：所有类型和函数。"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:228
msgid "[rewrite design](../design/rewrite.md) for rewriting theory, the one-redex contract and the normal-form lemma."
msgstr "[rewrite 设计](../design/rewrite.md)：重写理论、单可约式契约与范式引理。"

#: manual/tutorial/rewrite.md:230
msgid "[eval tutorial](eval.md) for named reduction strategies."
msgstr "[eval 教程](eval.md)：具名归约策略。"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:1
msgid "stlc tutorial"
msgstr "stlc 教程"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:3
msgid "This tutorial type-checks simply typed lambda terms, explains type errors, normalizes well-typed terms, and decides whether two terms are equal up to beta and eta. Terms are the shared `@syntax.Term[@stlc.Atom]`, so everything you know from [syntax](syntax.md) applies."
msgstr "本教程对简单类型 lambda 项做类型检查、解释类型错误、对良类型项做范式化，并判定两个项在 beta 和 eta 意义下是否相等。项使用共享的 `@syntax.Term[@stlc.Atom]`，因此你从 [syntax](syntax.md) 学到的一切都适用。"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:10
msgid "declare typed constants and variables"
msgstr "声明带类型的常量和变量"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:11
msgid "find the type of a term"
msgstr "求项的类型"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:12
msgid "check a function against its type"
msgstr "对照类型检查函数"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:13
msgid "get the canonical normal form"
msgstr "获得规范的范式"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:14
msgid "decide whether two terms are beta-eta equal"
msgstr "判定两个项是否 β-η 相等"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:14
msgid "compare their eta-long forms with `@syntax.alpha_equal`"
msgstr "用 `@syntax.alpha_equal` 比较它们的 η-长形式"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:15
msgid "normalize step by step with a count"
msgstr "带计数地逐步范式化"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:32
msgid "Check the identity function against $A \\to A$:"
msgstr "用 $A \\to A$ 检查恒等函数："

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:51
msgid "These helpers keep the examples short:"
msgstr "以下辅助函数让示例保持简短："

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:83
msgid "Declare constants and variables"
msgstr "声明常量和变量"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:85
msgid "A `Signature` types the constants of your language, a `TypeContext` the free variables of the term being checked. Applications are then inferred:"
msgstr "`Signature` 为语言中的常量指定类型，`TypeContext` 为被检查项的自由变量指定类型。这样应用的类型就可以推断出来："

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:100
msgid "Explain a type error"
msgstr "解释类型错误"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:102
msgid "Every rejection is a `TypeError` value you can match on and report:"
msgstr "每次拒绝都是一个 `TypeError` 值，你可以对它做模式匹配并报告："

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:135
msgid "Check functions against their types"
msgstr "用类型检查函数"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:137
msgid "Lambdas are checked, not inferred: give the expected type and the checker pushes it into the body."
msgstr "lambda 是被检查的，而不是被推断的：给出期望类型，检查器会把它推入函数体。"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:155
msgid "A redex is checked in the same way when it returns a lambda: the checker infers the type of the argument, gives it to the parameter, and checks the returned lambda against the expected type."
msgstr "可约式返回 lambda 时也以同样的方式检查：检查器推断参数的类型，把它赋给形参，再把返回的 lambda 对照期望类型进行检查。"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:176
msgid "Normalize a well-typed term"
msgstr "范式化良类型项"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:178
msgid "`normalize_eta_long` returns the canonical form: beta-normal, and every function-typed subterm written as a lambda."
msgstr "`normalize_eta_long` 返回规范形式：beta 范式，且每个函数类型的子项都写成 lambda。"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:196
msgid "The redex $(\\lambda h.\\,h)\\,g$ is inferred by giving `h` the type of `g`."
msgstr "可约式 $(\\lambda h.\\,h)\\,g$ 的类型通过给 `h` 赋予 `g` 的类型来推断。"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:198
msgid "Decide beta-eta equality"
msgstr "判定 beta-eta 相等"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:200
msgid "Two well-typed terms of the same type are $\\beta\\eta$-equal exactly when their eta-long normal forms are alpha-equivalent:"
msgstr "两个同类型的良类型项 $\\beta\\eta$-相等，当且仅当它们的 η-长形式范式 α-等价："

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:232
msgid "Operational normalization with a trace"
msgstr "带轨迹的操作式范式化"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:234
msgid "`normalize_checked` type-checks and then runs the untyped normal-order beta-eta reducer, which gives eta-*short* results and step counts. Use it when you want the reference semantics:"
msgstr "`normalize_checked` 先做类型检查，再运行无类型的正规序 beta-eta 归约器，它给出 eta-*短*的结果和步数。需要参考语义时使用它："

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:251
msgid "For a full trace, check the term and call `@eval.trace` with `@lambda.beta_eta_rule` yourself."
msgstr "要获得完整轨迹，请自行检查项，并用 `@lambda.beta_eta_rule` 调用 `@eval.trace`。"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:254
msgid "Use the substrate on typed terms"
msgstr "在带类型的项上使用底层库"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:256
msgid "Because `@stlc.Term` is `@syntax.Term[@stlc.Atom]`, substitution, free variables and rewriting work unchanged. Substituting a well-typed term of the right type for a variable preserves typing (the substitution lemma of typed calculi), so you can instantiate a typed template with `@substitution.Substitution` and re-check it."
msgstr "由于 `@stlc.Term` 就是 `@syntax.Term[@stlc.Atom]`，代换、自由变量和重写都可原样使用。用类型正确的良类型项代换变量会保持类型（类型化演算的代换引理），因此你可以用 `@substitution.Substitution` 实例化带类型的模板，再重新检查。"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:264
msgid "**Inferring a lambda.** `infer` on a lambda fails with `CannotInferLambda`. Use `check` with the expected type."
msgstr "**推断 lambda。** 对 lambda 调用 `infer` 会以 `CannotInferLambda` 失败。请用带期望类型的 `check`。"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:266
msgid "**Unit eta.** A neutral term of type `Unit`, such as a variable `u : Unit`, is not replaced by `()`. `f u` and `f ()` have different normal forms."
msgstr "**Unit 的 eta。** `Unit` 类型的中性项（例如变量 `u : Unit`）不会被替换为 `()`。`f u` 和 `f ()` 的范式不同。"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:268
msgid "**Empty applications.** `Apply(f, [])` is rejected with `EmptyApplication`, also inside a spine such as `Apply(Apply(f, []), [a])`. Build applications with at least one argument."
msgstr "**空应用。** `Apply(f, [])` 会以 `EmptyApplication` 被拒绝，包括出现在脊内部的情形，例如 `Apply(Apply(f, []), [a])`。构造应用时至少给一个参数。"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:271
msgid "**Comparing normal forms with `==`.** Generated binders are `x`, `x_1`, …; compare with `@syntax.alpha_equal`."
msgstr "**用 `==` 比较范式。** 生成的绑定子是 `x`、`x_1`、…；请用 `@syntax.alpha_equal` 比较。"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:276
msgid "[stlc API](../api/stlc.md) for all types, errors and functions."
msgstr "[stlc API](../api/stlc.md)：所有类型、错误和函数。"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:277
msgid "[stlc design](../design/stlc.md) for the typing rules, the eta-long normal forms and the correctness argument of typed NbE."
msgstr "[stlc 设计](../design/stlc.md)：定型规则、η-长形式范式，以及带类型 NbE 的正确性论证。"

#: manual/tutorial/stlc.md:279
msgid "[utlc/nbe tutorial](utlc/nbe.md) for the untyped, fuel-bounded counterpart."
msgstr "[utlc/nbe 教程](utlc/nbe.md)：无类型、受燃料限制的对应物。"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:1
msgid "substitution tutorial"
msgstr "substitution 教程"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:3
msgid "This tutorial replaces variables by terms: instantiating a template, swapping variables, substituting under binders without capturing anything, composing substitutions and evaluating partially. The examples encode arithmetic as `Term[String]`, with operators as values: $x + 1$ is `Apply(Value(\"+\"), [Variable(x), Value(\"1\")])`."
msgstr "本教程用项替换变量：实例化模板、交换变量、在绑定子之下代换而不捕获任何东西、复合代换以及部分求值。示例把算术编码为 `Term[String]`，运算符作为值：$x + 1$ 是 `Apply(Value(\"+\"), [Variable(x), Value(\"1\")])`。"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:11
msgid "replace one variable by a term"
msgstr "用一个项替换一个变量"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:12
msgid "replace several variables at once"
msgstr "同时替换多个变量"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:13
msgid "substitute one substitution after another in one pass"
msgstr "在一趟中先后执行两个代换"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:14
msgid "keep only the entries that matter"
msgstr "只保留起作用的条目"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:15
msgid "substitute in my own AST"
msgstr "在我自己的 AST 中代换"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:31
msgid "Substitute $2$ for $x$ in $x + 1$:"
msgstr "在 $x + 1$ 中用 $2$ 代换 $x$："

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:44
msgid "The examples below share two helpers:"
msgstr "下面的示例共用两个辅助函数："

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:56
msgid "Swap two variables"
msgstr "交换两个变量"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:58
msgid "All entries of a substitution apply at the same time, so a swap needs no temporary variable:"
msgstr "代换的所有条目同时生效，因此交换不需要临时变量："

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:71
msgid "Substitute under a binder"
msgstr "在绑定子之下代换"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:73
msgid "Substituting $y$ for $x$ in $\\lambda y.\\, x + y$ must not turn the inserted $y$ into the bound one. The binder is renamed to `y_1`:"
msgstr "在 $\\lambda y.\\, x + y$ 中用 $y$ 代换 $x$ 时，不能让插入的 $y$ 变成被约束的那个。绑定子会被重命名为 `y_1`："

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:89
msgid "A binder for the substituted variable itself shadows it, so nothing happens inside:"
msgstr "被代换变量自身的绑定子会遮蔽它，因此内部什么也不会发生："

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:103
msgid "Substitute the variables you know and leave the others in place:"
msgstr "代换已知的变量，其余变量保持原位："

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:116
msgid "Compose substitutions"
msgstr "复合代换"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:118
msgid "`first.then(second)` is one substitution that does `first` and then `second`. It is applied in a single traversal:"
msgstr "`first.then(second)` 是先做 `first` 再做 `second` 的单个代换。它在一次遍历中完成："

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:136
msgid "Implement beta reduction"
msgstr "实现 beta 归约"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:138
msgid "Beta reduction $(\\lambda x.\\,b)\\,a \\to b[x := a]$ is one substitution. This is how [`@lambda.beta_rule`](../api/utlc/lambda.md) works:"
msgstr "Beta 归约 $(\\lambda x.\\,b)\\,a \\to b[x := a]$ 就是一次代换。[`@lambda.beta_rule`](../api/utlc/lambda.md) 正是这样工作的："

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:160
msgid "Iterate to a fixed point yourself"
msgstr "自行迭代到不动点"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:162
msgid "A substitution is applied once. If replacements may mention variables of the domain and you want those replaced too, apply repeatedly, with a bound, because the process need not terminate (think of $x := x + 1$):"
msgstr "代换只应用一次。如果替换内容可能提及定义域中的变量，而你也希望它们被替换，就要重复应用，并设定上限，因为这个过程未必终止（想想 $x := x + 1$）："

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:192
msgid "Substitute in your own AST"
msgstr "在你自己的 AST 中代换"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:194
msgid "`GenericSubstitution` runs the same algorithm on any AST that implements `@syntax.BindingSyntax`. The [adapter tutorial](adapter.md) defines such an AST and substitutes in it with `apply_once`."
msgstr "`GenericSubstitution` 在任何实现了 `@syntax.BindingSyntax` 的 AST 上运行相同的算法。[adapter 教程](adapter.md)定义了这样一个 AST，并用 `apply_once` 在其中代换。"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:200
msgid "**Ambiguous constructors.** `@syntax.Variable(y)` is ambiguous when no type is expected, because `BindingView` also has a `Variable` case. Write `@syntax.Term::Variable(y)`, or annotate the expected type."
msgstr "**有歧义的构造子。** 没有期望类型时 `@syntax.Variable(y)` 有歧义，因为 `BindingView` 也有一个 `Variable` 分支。请写 `@syntax.Term::Variable(y)`，或标注期望类型。"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:203
msgid "**Expecting repeated substitution.** $\\{x \\mapsto y,\\ y \\mapsto 7\\}$ applied to $x$ gives $y$, not $7$. Use `then` or iterate explicitly."
msgstr "**期望重复代换。** $\\{x \\mapsto y,\\ y \\mapsto 7\\}$ 作用于 $x$ 得到 $y$，而不是 $7$。请使用 `then` 或显式迭代。"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:205
msgid "**Comparing with `==`.** Results may contain renamed binders (`y_1`). Compare with `@syntax.alpha_equal` unless you know the exact names."
msgstr "**用 `==` 比较。** 结果可能包含被重命名的绑定子（`y_1`）。除非你知道确切的名，否则请用 `@syntax.alpha_equal` 比较。"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:207
msgid "**Variables inside values.** `Value` payloads are not substituted into."
msgstr "**值内部的变量。** 不会对 `Value` 的载荷进行代换。"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:211
msgid "[substitution API](../api/substitution.md) for every function."
msgstr "[substitution API](../api/substitution.md)：所有函数。"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:212
msgid "[substitution design](../design/substitution.md) for the definition and the composition and substitution lemmas."
msgstr "[substitution 设计](../design/substitution.md)：定义以及复合引理和代换引理。"

#: manual/tutorial/substitution.md:214
msgid "[rewrite tutorial](rewrite.md) to apply rules, built from substitution, anywhere in a term."
msgstr "[rewrite 教程](rewrite.md)：在项的任意位置应用由代换构建的规则。"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:1
msgid "syntax tutorial"
msgstr "syntax 教程"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:3
msgid "This tutorial builds terms with binders using `Term[T]`, prints them, asks which variables are free, compares terms up to the names of bound variables and renames variables without capture. At the end you write an analysis that works for any AST implementing `BindingSyntax`."
msgstr "本教程用 `Term[T]` 构建带绑定子的项、打印它们、询问哪些变量是自由的、在约束变量名不计的意义下比较项，并在不发生捕获的情况下重命名变量。最后你会编写一个适用于任何实现了 `BindingSyntax` 的 AST 的分析。"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:10
msgid "build a term with binders"
msgstr "构建带绑定子的项"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:10
msgid "the constructors of `@syntax.Term`"
msgstr "`@syntax.Term` 的构造子"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:11
msgid "list the free variables, or every name"
msgstr "列出自由变量或所有名字"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:12
msgid "compare terms up to bound names"
msgstr "不计约束名差异地比较项"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:13
msgid "rename free variables without capture"
msgstr "无捕获地重命名自由变量"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:14
msgid "change the type of the constants"
msgstr "改变常量的类型"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:15
msgid "write one analysis for every binding-aware AST"
msgstr "为每个感知绑定的 AST 编写同一份分析"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:15
msgid "functions bounded by `BindingSyntax`"
msgstr "以 `BindingSyntax` 为约束的函数"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:30
msgid "The identity function $\\lambda x.\\,x$ has no free variables; $\\lambda x.\\,y$ has one:"
msgstr "恒等函数 $\\lambda x.\\,x$ 没有自由变量；$\\lambda x.\\,y$ 有一个："

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:46
msgid "Build terms with small helpers"
msgstr "用小型辅助函数构建项"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:48
msgid "Writing `@core.Name::new` everywhere gets noisy. Define helpers once:"
msgstr "到处写 `@core.Name::new` 会很啰嗦。一次性定义辅助函数："

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:70
msgid "Print a term"
msgstr "打印项"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:72
msgid "`Term` has no text format of its own, because the right notation depends on the language it encodes. A printer for lambda notation is a short recursive function:"
msgstr "`Term` 没有自己的文本格式，因为合适的记法取决于它所编码的语言。lambda 记法的打印器是一个简短的递归函数："

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:98
msgid "`==` compares terms literally. `alpha_equal` ignores the names of bound variables, which is almost always what you want:"
msgstr "`==` 按字面比较项。`alpha_equal` 忽略约束变量的名，这几乎总是你想要的："

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:112
msgid "Rename free variables safely"
msgstr "安全地重命名自由变量"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:114
msgid "Renaming `x` to `y` in $\\lambda y.\\,x$ must not produce $\\lambda y.\\,y$. `rename_free` renames the binder first:"
msgstr "在 $\\lambda y.\\,x$ 中把 `x` 重命名为 `y` 不能得到 $\\lambda y.\\,y$。`rename_free` 会先重命名绑定子："

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:129
msgid "The free `x` became `y`, and the binder became `y_1` so that the new `y` stays free."
msgstr "自由的 `x` 变成了 `y`，而绑定子变成了 `y_1`，使新的 `y` 保持自由。"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:132
msgid "Change the type of the constants"
msgstr "改变常量的类型"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:134
msgid "`map_values` converts constants and leaves the binding structure alone. Here integer literals become floating-point literals:"
msgstr "`map_values` 转换常量，不改动绑定结构。这里整数字面量变成浮点字面量："

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:148
msgid "Write an analysis for every binding-aware AST"
msgstr "为所有感知绑定的 AST 编写分析"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:150
msgid "Functions written against `BindingSyntax` work for `Term[T]` and for any downstream AST that implements the trait. This one counts binders:"
msgstr "针对 `BindingSyntax` 编写的函数既适用于 `Term[T]`，也适用于任何实现了该 trait 的下游 AST。下面这个函数统计绑定子个数："

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:170
msgid "The [adapter tutorial](adapter.md) implements `BindingSyntax` for a custom AST, after which `count_binders`, generic substitution and generic rewriting all apply to it."
msgstr "[adapter 教程](adapter.md)为自定义 AST 实现了 `BindingSyntax`，之后 `count_binders`、泛型代换和泛型重写都能应用于它。"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:174
msgid "Rename a binder by hand"
msgstr "手动重命名绑定子"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:176
msgid "When you build a binder from parts, `alpha_rename_bound` changes the name of its variable, and refuses a name that is already used in the body:"
msgstr "当你从部件构建绑定子时，`alpha_rename_bound` 会改变其变量的名，并拒绝已在体中使用的名："

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:199
msgid "**`==` is not alpha-equivalence.** Results of substitution and normalization may have renamed binders such as `y_1`. Compare them with `alpha_equal`."
msgstr "**`==` 不是 α-等价。** 代换和范式化的结果可能含有被重命名的绑定子，例如 `y_1`。请用 `alpha_equal` 比较。"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:202
msgid "**Payloads are compared with their own `==`.** `alpha_equal` inherits it: with `Term[Double]`, a term containing `Value(0.0 / 0.0)` (NaN) is not alpha-equal to itself, and `Value(0.0)` equals `Value(-0.0)`."
msgstr "**载荷用其自身的 `==` 比较。** `alpha_equal` 继承它：对 `Term[Double]`，含 `Value(0.0 / 0.0)`（NaN）的项与自身不 α-相等，而 `Value(0.0)` 等于 `Value(-0.0)`。"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:205
msgid "**Variables inside values.** `Value(T)` is never inspected. If your constants contain variables, implement `BindingSyntax` for your AST instead of wrapping it in `Term`."
msgstr "**值内部的变量。** `Value(T)` 从不被检查。如果你的常量包含变量，请为你的 AST 实现 `BindingSyntax`，而不是把它包装进 `Term`。"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:208
msgid "**Calling `alpha_rename_bound` on the binder.** It expects the *body*: `body.alpha_rename_bound(x, z)`, not `Bind(x, body).alpha_rename_bound(...)`, which would find no free `x` to rename."
msgstr "**对绑定子调用 `alpha_rename_bound`。** 它期望的是*体*：`body.alpha_rename_bound(x, z)`，而不是 `Bind(x, body).alpha_rename_bound(...)`，后者找不到可重命名的自由 `x`。"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:211
msgid "**Method-style trait calls.** `term.project()` is deprecated; write `@syntax.BindingSyntax::project(term)`."
msgstr "**方法风格的 trait 调用。** `term.project()` 已弃用；请写 `@syntax.BindingSyntax::project(term)`。"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:216
msgid "[syntax API](../api/syntax.md): every function and its contract."
msgstr "[syntax API](../api/syntax.md)：每个函数及其契约。"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:217
msgid "[syntax design](../design/syntax.md): the definitions and the proofs behind alpha-equivalence and capture-avoiding renaming."
msgstr "[syntax 设计](../design/syntax.md)：α-等价与避免捕获的重命名背后的定义和证明。"

#: manual/tutorial/syntax.md:219
msgid "[substitution tutorial](substitution.md): replacing variables by terms."
msgstr "[substitution 教程](substitution.md)：用项替换变量。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:1
msgid "utlc/lambda tutorial"
msgstr "utlc/lambda 教程"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:3
msgid "This tutorial computes with the untyped lambda calculus: it builds terms, normalizes them with beta and eta, encodes booleans and numbers as functions, and deals with terms that never stop reducing."
msgstr "本教程使用无类型 lambda 演算进行计算：构建项、用 beta 和 eta 对其范式化、把布尔值和数编码为函数，并处理永不停止归约的项。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:9
msgid "build $\\lambda x.\\,b$ and $f\\,a$"
msgstr "构建 $\\lambda x.\\,b$ 与 $f\\,a$"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:10
msgid "compute a beta-eta normal form"
msgstr "计算 β-η 范式"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:11
msgid "use beta or eta alone, or another strategy"
msgstr "单独使用 β 或 η，或使用其他策略"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:11
msgid "`beta_rule`, `eta_rule` with `@eval.evaluate`"
msgstr "`beta_rule`、`eta_rule` 配合 `@eval.evaluate`"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:12
msgid "stop on terms that do not terminate"
msgstr "在不终止的项上停下来"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:12
msgid "the step limit and `StepLimitReached`"
msgstr "步数上限与 `StepLimitReached`"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:40
msgid "The tasks use a few helpers to keep terms short:"
msgstr "这些任务用几个辅助函数让项保持简短："

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:63
msgid "Encode booleans"
msgstr "编码布尔值"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:65
msgid "Church booleans choose between two arguments: $\\mathsf{true} = \\lambda t.\\,\\lambda f.\\,t$, $\\mathsf{false} = \\lambda t.\\,\\lambda f.\\,f$, and $\\mathsf{if}\\;b\\;x\\;y = b\\,x\\,y$."
msgstr "Church 布尔值在两个参数之间做选择：$\\mathsf{true} = \\lambda t.\\,\\lambda f.\\,t$，$\\mathsf{false} = \\lambda t.\\,\\lambda f.\\,f$，且 $\\mathsf{if}\\;b\\;x\\;y = b\\,x\\,y$。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:79
msgid "Encode numbers and add them"
msgstr "编码数并相加"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:81
msgid "The Church numeral $n$ applies a function $n$ times: $\\overline{2} = \\lambda f.\\,\\lambda x.\\,f\\,(f\\,x)$. Addition is $\\lambda m.\\,\\lambda n.\\,\\lambda f.\\,\\lambda x.\\,m\\,f\\,(n\\,f\\,x)$."
msgstr "Church 数 $n$ 把函数应用 $n$ 次：$\\overline{2} = \\lambda f.\\,\\lambda x.\\,f\\,(f\\,x)$。加法是 $\\lambda m.\\,\\lambda n.\\,\\lambda f.\\,\\lambda x.\\,m\\,f\\,(n\\,f\\,x)$。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:104
msgid "Normal forms may use different binder names (`f_1`, …) from your expectation; `alpha_equal` ignores them."
msgstr "范式使用的绑定子名（`f_1`、…）可能与你预期的不同；`alpha_equal` 会忽略它们。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:107
msgid "Use eta to simplify wrappers"
msgstr "用 eta 简化包装"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:109
msgid "$\\lambda x.\\,g\\,x$ is just $g$ when $x$ is not free in $g$. `normalize` removes such wrappers:"
msgstr "当 $x$ 不在 $g$ 中自由出现时，$\\lambda x.\\,g\\,x$ 就是 $g$。`normalize` 会去掉这样的包装："

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:124
msgid "Handle terms that do not terminate"
msgstr "处理不终止的项"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:126
msgid "$\\Omega = (\\lambda w.\\,w\\,w)(\\lambda w.\\,w\\,w)$ reduces to itself forever. The step limit turns that into a result you can test for:"
msgstr "$\\Omega = (\\lambda w.\\,w\\,w)(\\lambda w.\\,w\\,w)$ 永远归约到自身。步数上限把这变成一个你可以检测的结果："

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:144
msgid "Only beta, or another strategy"
msgstr "只用 beta，或换一种策略"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:146
msgid "`normalize` fixes beta-eta and normal order. For other combinations, pass a rule and a strategy to `@eval.evaluate` (import `Luna-Flow/type_theory/eval`):"
msgstr "`normalize` 固定使用 beta-eta 和正规序。对于其他组合，把规则和策略传给 `@eval.evaluate`（导入 `Luna-Flow/type_theory/eval`）："

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:163
msgid "Beta alone under weak head stops at $\\lambda y.\\,g\\,y$; `normalize` would also eta-reduce it to $g$."
msgstr "弱头策略下只用 beta 会停在 $\\lambda y.\\,g\\,y$；`normalize` 还会把它 eta 归约为 $g$。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:166
msgid "Domain values"
msgstr "领域值"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:168
msgid "`Value(v)` is a constant that never reduces and is copied by substitution. Add reduction rules for constants (such as arithmetic on `Value(Int)`) with your own rule, and combine it with `beta_rule` as shown in the [rewrite tutorial](../rewrite.md)."
msgstr "`Value(v)` 是一个从不归约、在代换中被复制的常量。用你自己的规则为常量添加归约规则（例如 `Value(Int)` 上的算术），并按 [rewrite 教程](../rewrite.md)所示把它与 `beta_rule` 组合。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:173
msgid "Faster normalization"
msgstr "更快的范式化"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:175
msgid "Normal-order reduction on named terms renames binders and repeats searches from the root. For large terms, convert with `@debruijn.from_named` and use [utlc/nbe](nbe.md)."
msgstr "具名项上的正规序归约会重命名绑定子，并从根部重复搜索。对于大型项，请用 `@debruijn.from_named` 转换并使用 [utlc/nbe](nbe.md)。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:181
msgid "**n-ary applications and eta.** `Apply(f, [a, x])` under `Bind(x, …)` is not eta-reduced; build applications with `application` (unary) if you rely on eta."
msgstr "**n 元应用与 eta。** `Bind(x, …)` 之下的 `Apply(f, [a, x])` 不会被 eta 归约；如果依赖 eta，请用 `application`（一元）构建应用。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:184
msgid "**Comparing with `==`.** Beta renames binders to avoid capture; use `@syntax.alpha_equal`."
msgstr "**用 `==` 比较。** beta 会重命名绑定子以避免捕获；请使用 `@syntax.alpha_equal`。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:186
msgid "**Reading `StepLimitReached` as divergence.** It only means the limit was reached. Normalizing terms can need many steps."
msgstr "**把 `StepLimitReached` 理解为发散。** 它只表示达到了上限。可范式化的项也可能需要很多步。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:188
msgid "**Expecting constants to compute.** `Value(1)` applied to anything stays stuck; the calculus has no built-in arithmetic."
msgstr "**期望常量会计算。** `Value(1)` 作用于任何东西都会卡住；该演算没有内置算术。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:193
msgid "[utlc/lambda API](../../api/utlc/lambda.md) for the exact contracts."
msgstr "[utlc/lambda API](../../api/utlc/lambda.md)：精确的契约。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:194
msgid "[utlc/lambda design](../../design/utlc/lambda.md) for beta, eta and the classical theorems."
msgstr "[utlc/lambda 设计](../../design/utlc/lambda.md)：beta、eta 以及经典定理。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/lambda.md:196
msgid "[stlc tutorial](../stlc.md) for the typed calculus, where every term normalizes."
msgstr "[stlc 教程](../stlc.md)：每个项都可范式化的带类型演算。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:1
msgid "utlc/nbe tutorial"
msgstr "utlc/nbe 教程"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:3
msgid "This tutorial normalizes untyped lambda terms with normalization by evaluation: fast normal forms of De Bruijn terms within a fuel budget. You will normalize terms written with names, pick a budget, read the `consumed` counter, and compare results with the small-step reducer."
msgstr "本教程用基于求值的范式化来范式化无类型 lambda 项：在燃料预算内快速得到 De Bruijn 项的范式。你将范式化用名书写的项、选择预算、读取 `consumed` 计数器，并将结果与小步归约器比较。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:10
msgid "normalize a De Bruijn term quickly"
msgstr "快速范式化 De Bruijn 项"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:11
msgid "normalize a named term"
msgstr "范式化具名项"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:11
msgid "`@debruijn.from_named`, then `normalize`, then `@debruijn.to_named`"
msgstr "`@debruijn.from_named`，然后 `normalize`，然后 `@debruijn.to_named`"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:12
msgid "bound the work on a term that may diverge"
msgstr "限制可能发散的项上的工作量"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:12
msgid "the fuel argument and `FuelExhausted`"
msgstr "燃料参数与 `FuelExhausted`"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:13
msgid "evaluate once and read back later"
msgstr "求值一次，稍后读回"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:13
msgid "`eval`, then `quote`"
msgstr "`eval`，然后 `quote`"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:14
msgid "read back a free variable"
msgstr "读回自由变量"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:46
msgid "Normalize a named term"
msgstr "范式化具名项"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:48
msgid "Write terms with names, convert them with `from_named`, normalize, and convert back for display:"
msgstr "用名书写项，用 `from_named` 转换，范式化，再转换回来以便显示："

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:79
msgid "Comparing De Bruijn forms with `==` is comparing up to alpha-equivalence."
msgstr "用 `==` 比较 De Bruijn 形式就是在 α-等价意义下比较。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:81
msgid "Choose a fuel budget"
msgstr "选择燃料预算"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:83
msgid "Fuel bounds the work, not the time. Too little fuel gives `FuelExhausted`; the `consumed` value of a successful run is the exact amount that run needs:"
msgstr "燃料限制的是工作量，而不是时间。燃料太少会得到 `FuelExhausted`；成功运行的 `consumed` 值正是该次运行所需的确切数量："

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:100
msgid "Recognise divergence and laziness"
msgstr "识别发散与惰性"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:102
msgid "$\\Omega$ never reaches a normal form, so it always exhausts the budget. An argument that is never used is never evaluated, so passing $\\Omega$ to a constant function is fine:"
msgstr "$\\Omega$ 永远不会到达范式，因此总会耗尽预算。从不使用的参数从不被求值，因此把 $\\Omega$ 传给常函数是没问题的："

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:116
msgid "Reject ill-scoped input"
msgstr "拒绝作用域不正确的输入"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:118
msgid "`normalize` validates first and reports a dangling index as data:"
msgstr "`normalize` 先做校验，并把悬空索引作为数据报告："

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:132
msgid "Compare with small-step reduction"
msgstr "与小步归约比较"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:134
msgid "NbE returns unary applications; `@debruijn.normalize` keeps n-ary spines. Flatten spines before comparing:"
msgstr "NbE 返回一元应用；`@debruijn.normalize` 保留 n 元脊。比较前先展平脊："

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:169
msgid "Use the pipeline directly"
msgstr "直接使用流水线"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:171
msgid "`eval` produces an opaque semantic value; `quote` reads it back. Splitting the two is useful to evaluate once and quote at a chosen level, or to quote neutral values made with `reflect_free`:"
msgstr "`eval` 产生不透明的语义值；`quote` 将其读回。把两者分开很有用：可以只求值一次再在选定的层级读回，或读回用 `reflect_free` 构造的中性值："

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:188
msgid "**Comparing with the small-step result by `==`.** Spine shapes differ; flatten first."
msgstr "**用 `==` 与小步结果比较。** 脊的形状不同；请先展平。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:190
msgid "**Treating `FuelExhausted` as divergence.** It only says the budget ran out. Raise the budget or use the typed [stlc](../stlc.md) normalizer, which needs no budget."
msgstr "**把 `FuelExhausted` 当作发散。** 它只说明预算用完了。请提高预算，或使用不需要预算的带类型 [stlc](../stlc.md) 范式化器。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:193
msgid "**Duplicated arguments.** Evaluation is call by name without sharing; a term that uses an expensive argument many times pays for it each time."
msgstr "**重复的参数。** 求值是无共享的传名调用；多次使用某个昂贵参数的项每次都要为它付出代价。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:195
msgid "**Open terms with dangling indices.** Free variables must be `Free(name)`; a `Bound` index without a binder is a scope error."
msgstr "**带悬空索引的开项。** 自由变量必须是 `Free(name)`；没有绑定子的 `Bound` 索引是作用域错误。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:200
msgid "[utlc/nbe API](../../api/utlc/nbe.md) for every type and function."
msgstr "[utlc/nbe API](../../api/utlc/nbe.md)：所有类型和函数。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:201
msgid "[utlc/nbe design](../../design/utlc/nbe.md) for the semantic domain and the soundness argument."
msgstr "[utlc/nbe 设计](../../design/utlc/nbe.md)：语义域与可靠性论证。"

#: manual/tutorial/utlc/nbe.md:203
msgid "[stlc tutorial](../stlc.md) for typed, eta-long NbE."
msgstr "[stlc 教程](../stlc.md)：带类型的 η-长形式 NbE。"

#~ msgid "A lambda checks against an arrow type by checking its body against the codomain, with the parameter given the domain. Every other term is inferred and compared with `==`; a difference gives `TypeMismatch`."
#~ msgstr "lambda 对照箭头类型进行检查时，会以定义域作为参数的类型，将体对照陪域进行检查。其他所有项都先推断类型，再用 `==` 比较；若不同则给出 `TypeMismatch`。"

#~ msgid "`check` accepts every well-typed beta-normal term."
#~ msgstr "`check` 接受每个良类型的 β-范式项。"

#~ msgid "**Divergence.** Untyped terms need not normalize, so every phase must be bounded."
#~ msgstr "**发散。** 无类型项不一定能范式化，因此每个阶段都必须有界。"

#~ msgid "**Agreement with small-step reduction.** By soundness and confluence, whenever both `@nbe.normalize` and `@debruijn.normalize` return a normal form for the same well-scoped term, the two normal forms are equal after spine flattening, which merges nested applications and drops empty ones. Both read `Apply(h, [])` as $h$: evaluation erases the node, and the small-step reducer looks through it when it matches a redex (see the [eval design](../eval.md)). The tests in `src/utlc/nbe/nbe_test.mbt` check this, laziness on $(\\lambda.\\,7)\\,\\Omega$, fuel exhaustion on $\\Omega$, and that quote turns levels back into indices."
#~ msgstr "**与小步归约一致。** 由可靠性与合流性，只要 `@nbe.normalize` 与 `@debruijn.normalize` 对同一个良作用域项都返回范式，两个范式在脊展平（合并嵌套的应用并去掉空应用）之后相等。两者都把 `Apply(h, [])` 读作 $h$：求值会抹去该节点，小步归约器在匹配可约式时透过它（见 [eval 设计](../eval.md)）。`src/utlc/nbe/nbe_test.mbt` 中的测试检查这一点，以及 $(\\lambda.\\,7)\\,\\Omega$ 上的惰性、$\\Omega$ 上的燃料耗尽，以及 quote 把层级转回索引。"

#~ msgid "`NegativeShift(index, delta, cutoff)`: shifting `Bound(index)` by `delta` would make it negative; `cutoff` is the effective cutoff at the occurrence."
#~ msgstr "`NegativeShift(index, delta, cutoff)`：将 `Bound(index)` 移位 `delta` 会使其变为负数；`cutoff` 是该出现处的有效截断值。"

#~ msgid "`shift(t, delta, cutoff)` is the operation $\\uparrow^{delta}_{cutoff}$: under `k` binders, an index `i >= cutoff + k` becomes `i + delta`, and smaller indices are left alone. Returns `Err(NegativeShift)` if an index would become negative and `Err(NegativeIndex)` if the input contains a negative index."
#~ msgstr "`shift(t, delta, cutoff)` 即操作 $\\uparrow^{delta}_{cutoff}$：在 `k` 个绑定子之下，索引 `i >= cutoff + k` 变为 `i + delta`，较小的索引保持不变。若某索引会变为负数则返回 `Err(NegativeShift)`，若输入包含负索引则返回 `Err(NegativeIndex)`。"

#~ msgid "`NoStep` and `Reduced` have the meaning of `@rewrite.StepResult`; the rule name is always `\"beta\"`. `ScopeFailure` reports an index error met while contracting a redex."
#~ msgstr "`NoStep` 和 `Reduced` 的含义与 `@rewrite.StepResult` 相同；规则名总是 `\"beta\"`。`ScopeFailure` 报告在收缩可约式时遇到的索引错误。"

#~ msgid "leftmost-innermost redex (`@rewrite.bottom_up_once`)"
#~ msgstr "最左最内可约式（`@rewrite.bottom_up_once`）"

#~ msgid "Children are tried before their parent, in the same left-to-right order. The chosen position is the leftmost-innermost redex. `NoStep` again means that the rule applies nowhere."
#~ msgstr "子节点先于其父节点尝试，顺序同样是从左到右。所选位置是最左最内的可约式。`NoStep` 同样表示该规则在任何位置都不适用。"

#~ msgid "Values are compared with `==`, free variables by name, and bound variables by the binder they refer to. The relation is an equivalence and is decided in one simultaneous traversal of both terms."
#~ msgstr "值用 `==` 比较，自由变量按名字比较，约束变量按其所指的绑定子比较。该关系是等价关系，并通过对两个项的一趟同时遍历来判定。"

#~ msgid "**Problem.** A negative shift on an ill-formed term yields a negative index, which silently refers to nothing."
#~ msgstr "**问题。** 对非良构项做负移位会产生负索引，它悄无声息地不指向任何东西。"

#~ msgid "**Choice.** `shift` returns `Err(NegativeShift)` instead, and `shift`, `substitute_bound`, `instantiate`, `validate` and `to_named` report `NegativeIndex` for any negative index they meet. The lemmas below show that the error cases are unreachable from well-scoped input, so the `Result` costs nothing for correct callers and turns a silent corruption into data for incorrect ones. This follows the library rule that expected failures at public boundaries are structured values."
#~ msgstr "**选择。** `shift` 改为返回 `Err(NegativeShift)`，并且 `shift`、`substitute_bound`、`instantiate`、`validate` 和 `to_named` 在遇到任何负索引时都报告 `NegativeIndex`。下面的引理表明，从良作用域的输入出发不可能到达错误情形，因此 `Result` 对正确的调用者没有代价，而对错误的调用者则把无声的损坏变成数据。这遵循本库的规则：公共边界上预期的失败是结构化的值。"

#~ msgid "No free index $0$ remains, so the shift by $-1$ maps $\\{1, \\dots, n\\} \\to \\{0, \\dots, n - 1\\}$ without a negative result. $\\square$"
#~ msgstr "不再有自由索引 $0$，因此按 $-1$ 的移位将 $\\{1, \\dots, n\\} \\to \\{0, \\dots, n - 1\\}$ 映射过去，不会产生负值。$\\square$"

#~ msgid "**No new semantics.** Every strategy is a traversal of [rewrite](rewrite.md), so it inherits the one-redex contract, the step-count contract and traces."
#~ msgstr "**不引入新语义。** 每个策略都是 [rewrite](rewrite.md) 的一种遍历，因此它继承单可约式契约、步数契约以及轨迹。"

#~ msgid "Each strategy is one traversal of rewrite"
#~ msgstr "每个策略都是 rewrite 的一种遍历"

#~ msgid "Pre-order search returns the first redex that no other redex contains, scanning head before arguments and arguments left to right; this is the leftmost-outermost redex, and the normal-form lemma of the [rewrite design](rewrite.md) shows that `NoStep` means \"normal\". Post-order search returns a redex that contains no other redex, the leftmost-innermost one. Weak head search follows only the spine, so its `NoStep` means \"weak head normal\" and nothing more."
#~ msgstr "前序搜索返回第一个不被其他可约式包含的可约式，先扫描头部再扫描参数，参数从左到右；这就是最左最外的可约式，而 [rewrite 设计](rewrite.md) 中的范式引理表明 `NoStep` 意味着\"已是范式\"。后序搜索返回一个不包含其他可约式的可约式，即最左最内的那个。弱头搜索只沿脊柱进行，因此它的 `NoStep` 仅意味着\"已是弱头范式\"，别无其他。"

#~ msgid "The library's tests check named and De Bruijn beta steps against each other (`src/utlc/lambda/lambda_test.mbt`), and normal order against the NbE normalizer (`src/utlc/nbe/nbe_test.mbt`)."
#~ msgstr "库的测试将具名与 De Bruijn 的 beta 步骤相互比对（`src/utlc/lambda/lambda_test.mbt`），并将正规序与 NbE 正规化器相互比对（`src/utlc/nbe/nbe_test.mbt`）。"

#~ msgid "has declarative type $B$ and no other. Without the renaming, the trailing $x$ would be typed in $\\Gamma, x{:}\\mathsf{Unit}$ and the checker would answer `Unit`; versions before the fix did exactly that, and `check` accepted the term at `Unit`. With $x' = x_1$ the trailing $x$ keeps its type $B$, and `infer` returns $B$. The typed evaluator computes the type of a redex head with the same rule, so `normalize_eta_long` accepts the same terms as `check`."
#~ msgstr "具有声明式类型 $B$，且没有其他类型。若不改名，后续的 $x$ 会在 $\\Gamma, x{:}\\mathsf{Unit}$ 中定型，检查器就会回答 `Unit`；修复之前的版本正是如此，`check` 曾在 `Unit` 下接受该项。取 $x' = x_1$ 后，后续的 $x$ 保持其类型 $B$，`infer` 返回 $B$。带类型的求值器用同一规则计算可约式头部的类型，因此 `normalize_eta_long` 与 `check` 接受相同的项。"

#~ msgid "The tests in `src/stlc/stlc_test.mbt` cover typing and rejection, shadowing, eta expansion of open variables and of constants (including nested arrow types and higher-order arguments), and agreement of the two normalizers on small terms."
#~ msgstr "`src/stlc/stlc_test.mbt` 中的测试覆盖了类型化与拒绝、遮蔽、开放变量和常量的 η-展开（包括嵌套箭头类型和高阶参数），以及两个范式化器在小项上的一致性。"

#~ msgid "**Choice.** `alpha_equal` walks both terms in lockstep with two binder environments $E_L, E_R$ that map each bound name to the *level* (binder depth, counting from the root) at which it was bound; a later binding of the same name shadows an earlier one. Writing $E(x)$ for the level of the last binding of $x$ in $E$, and $d$ for the current depth:"
#~ msgstr "**选择。** `alpha_equal` 以同步方式遍历两个项，并维护两个绑定环境 $E_L, E_R$，把每个约束名映射到它被绑定时的*层级*（绑定深度，从根开始计数）；同名的后续绑定会遮蔽先前的绑定。记 $E(x)$ 为 $E$ 中 $x$ 最后一次绑定的层级，$d$ 为当前深度："

#~ msgid "**Theorem.** `alpha_equal(t, u)` holds iff $t =_\\alpha u$."
#~ msgstr "**定理。** `alpha_equal(t, u)` 成立当且仅当 $t =_\\alpha u$。"

#~ msgid "*Proof sketch.* Let $\\ulcorner t \\urcorner$ be the De Bruijn translation of the [debruijn design](debruijn.md), which replaces a bound occurrence at depth $d$ whose binder sits at level $\\ell$ by the index $i = d - 1 - \\ell$, and keeps free names. Both traversals visit the same positions at the same depth $d$, so for bound occurrences"
#~ msgstr "*证明概要。* 设 $\\ulcorner t \\urcorner$ 为 [debruijn 设计](debruijn.md) 中的 De Bruijn 翻译，它把深度 $d$ 处、其绑定子位于层级 $\\ell$ 的约束出现替换为索引 $i = d - 1 - \\ell$，并保留自由名字。两种遍历在相同深度 $d$ 访问相同位置，因此对于约束出现"

#~ msgid "and free occurrences are compared by name in both. Hence `alpha_equal(t, u)` iff $\\ulcorner t \\urcorner = \\ulcorner u \\urcorner$. The classical theorem that two named terms are alpha-equivalent iff their De Bruijn translations are identical[^debruijn] completes the proof. $\\square$"
#~ msgstr "而自由出现在两者中都按名字比较。因此 `alpha_equal(t, u)` 当且仅当 $\\ulcorner t \\urcorner = \\ulcorner u \\urcorner$。经典定理指出两个具名项 α-等价当且仅当它们的 De Bruijn 翻译相同[^debruijn]，由此完成证明。$\\square$"

#~ msgid "`alpha_equal` is reflexive, symmetric and transitive, and coincides with $=_\\alpha$ (theorem above). Reflexivity is also checked by a QuickCheck property in `src/syntax/syntax_wbtest.mbt`."
#~ msgstr "`alpha_equal` 是自反、对称且传递的，并与 $=_\\alpha$ 一致（见上述定理）。自反性还由 `src/syntax/syntax_wbtest.mbt` 中的一个 QuickCheck 性质检验。"

#~ msgid "`normalize` returns a beta-eta normal form, which is in general *not* the beta normal form of the other normalizers: $\\lambda x.\\,f\\,x$ is beta-normal and normalizes to $f$ here. The two are related by eta alone. If $N$ is beta-normal, eta steps keep it beta-normal (a new beta redex would need $(\\lambda x.\\,f\\,x)\\,a$ or $\\lambda x.\\,(\\lambda y.\\,b)\\,x$ in $N$, both beta redexes already), so its eta normal form is beta-eta normal and, by confluence of $\\to_{\\beta\\eta}$, alpha-equivalent to the result of `normalize`, up to the unary-spine restriction of `eta_rule`."
#~ msgstr "`normalize` 返回 β-η 范式，它一般*不是*其他范式化器给出的 β 范式：$\\lambda x.\\,f\\,x$ 是 β-范式，而在这里范式化为 $f$。两者仅相差 η。若 $N$ 是 β-范式，η 步会保持其为 β-范式（新的 β 可约式需要 $N$ 中含有 $(\\lambda x.\\,f\\,x)\\,a$ 或 $\\lambda x.\\,(\\lambda y.\\,b)\\,x$，而两者本身已是 β 可约式），因此它的 η 范式是 β-η 范式，并且由 $\\to_{\\beta\\eta}$ 的合流性，与 `normalize` 的结果 α-等价；唯一的例外来自 `eta_rule` 仅处理一元脊这一限制。"

#~ msgid "An empty application `Apply(h, [])` is read as $h$ when a redex is matched, but it is not removed from the term (see the [eval design](../eval.md))."
#~ msgstr "空应用 `Apply(h, [])` 在匹配可约式时被读作 $h$，但不会从项中去掉（见 [eval 设计](../eval.md)）。"

#~ msgid "`@lambda.normalize` also contracts eta redexes, so its result is the eta normal form of that common beta normal form, not the beta normal form itself: $\\lambda x.\\,f\\,x$ normalizes to $f$ there and to $\\lambda.\\,f\\,0$ in the other two ([utlc/lambda design](design/utlc/lambda.md)). All normalizers read an empty application `Apply(h, [])` as $h$; NbE drops the node, the small-step reducers keep it, so spine flattening also drops empty applications ([eval design](design/eval.md))."
#~ msgstr "`@lambda.normalize` 还会收缩 eta 可约式，因此其结果是这个公共 beta 范式的 eta 范式，而不是该 beta 范式本身：$\\lambda x.\\,f\\,x$ 在那里范式化为 $f$，在另外两者中为 $\\lambda.\\,f\\,0$（[utlc/lambda 设计](design/utlc/lambda.md)）。所有范式化器都把空应用 `Apply(h, [])` 读作 $h$；NbE 去掉该节点，小步归约器保留它，因此脊展平也会去掉空应用（[eval 设计](design/eval.md)）。"

#~ msgid "`reduce_once` does not validate its input. It returns `ScopeFailure` only when the redex it contracts contains a negative index; a negative index elsewhere is skipped like any other variable, and a dangling index is shifted like a free one (`(λ. 5) 1` reduces to `Bound(4)`). Call `validate` first if the term may be ill scoped."
#~ msgstr "`reduce_once` 不验证其输入。仅当它收缩的可约式含有负索引时，它才返回 `ScopeFailure`；其他位置的负索引会像其他变量一样被跳过，悬空索引会像自由索引一样被移位（`(λ. 5) 1` 归约为 `Bound(4)`）。如果项可能作用域不良，请先调用 `validate`。"

#~ msgid "`ScopeFailure` carries the term on which the failing step was attempted and the number of steps taken before it."
#~ msgstr "`ScopeFailure` 携带尝试失败步骤时所在的项，以及在此之前已执行的步数。"

#~ msgid "It has the step-count contract of `@rewrite.normalize`: at most `max_steps` steps, and one extra `reduce_once` call to classify the final term. Like `reduce_once` it does not validate: on an ill-scoped input it may return `NormalForm` (for `Bind(Bound(-1))`, say), so `ScopeFailure` proves the input ill scoped but its absence proves nothing."
#~ msgstr "它遵循 `@rewrite.normalize` 的步数契约：最多 `max_steps` 步，并额外调用一次 `reduce_once` 来判定最终项。与 `reduce_once` 一样，它不做验证：对作用域不良的输入，它可能返回 `NormalForm`（例如对 `Bind(Bound(-1))`），因此 `ScopeFailure` 能证明输入作用域不良，但没有得到它并不能证明任何事。"

#~ msgid "[!WARNING] When a lambda is applied to two or more arguments, `infer` types the remaining arguments in a context that already contains the lambda's parameter. If one of those arguments mentions a free variable with the same name as the parameter, it is typed with the parameter's type, and the checker can then *accept a wrong type*. With `x : B` in the context, `check` accepts $(\\lambda x.\\,\\lambda y.\\,y)\\;()\\;x$ at `Unit` and rejects it at its real type `B`; `normalize_checked` then returns `x`, a term of type `B`, as a normal form \"of type `Unit`\". `normalize_eta_long` rejects the term at both types. Until this is fixed, make sure the parameter of such a redex does not occur free in the later arguments (rename it, or apply the arguments one at a time)."
#~ msgstr "[!WARNING] 当 lambda 被应用于两个或更多参数时，`infer` 会在已经包含该 lambda 形参的上下文中为其余参数确定类型。如果其中某个参数提到了与该形参同名的自由变量，它就会被赋予该形参的类型，于是检查器可能*接受错误的类型*。当上下文中有 `x : B` 时，`check` 在 `Unit` 下接受 $(\\lambda x.\\,\\lambda y.\\,y)\\;()\\;x$，却在其真实类型 `B` 下拒绝它；随后 `normalize_checked` 把类型为 `B` 的项 `x` 作为“类型为 `Unit`”的范式返回。`normalize_eta_long` 在两个类型下都拒绝该项。在此问题修复之前，请确保这类可约式的形参不在后续参数中自由出现（重命名该形参，或者逐个应用参数）。"

#~ msgid "The reducers check less. `reduce_once` looks at indices only inside the redex it contracts, through `instantiate`: a negative index elsewhere is passed over like a variable, and no operation except `validate` and `to_named` detects a dangling (too large) index, which `instantiate` shifts like a free one. Scope is checked once, by `validate`, not on every step."
#~ msgstr "归约器检查得更少。`reduce_once` 只通过 `instantiate` 查看它所收缩的可约式内部的索引：其他位置的负索引会像变量一样被略过；除 `validate` 和 `to_named` 外，没有任何操作检测悬空（过大的）索引，`instantiate` 会像对待自由索引一样对其移位。作用域只由 `validate` 检查一次，而不是每一步都检查。"

#~ msgid "`substitute_bound`, `instantiate`, `reduce_once` and `normalize` do not detect unbound indices, and the reducers ignore negative indices outside the redex they contract; call `validate` on untrusted input."
#~ msgstr "`substitute_bound`、`instantiate`、`reduce_once` 与 `normalize` 不检测未绑定的索引，且归约器会忽略其所收缩的可约式之外的负索引；对不可信输入请调用 `validate`。"

#~ msgid "An empty application `Apply(h, [])` is not a redex and blocks any redex in its head position (`Apply(Apply(Bind(b), []), [a])` is in normal form for `reduce_once`), while [utlc/nbe](utlc/nbe.md) erases it. Build applications with at least one argument."
#~ msgstr "空应用 `Apply(h, [])` 不是可约式，并会阻塞其头部位置上的任何可约式（对 `reduce_once` 而言，`Apply(Apply(Bind(b), []), [a])` 是范式），而 [utlc/nbe](utlc/nbe.md) 会将其消除。构造应用时请至少给出一个参数。"

#~ msgid "has declarative type $B$ and no other (the outer $x$ has type $B$), but `infer` types the second argument in $\\Gamma, x{:}\\mathsf{Unit}$ and returns `Unit`. Hence `check` succeeds at `Unit` and fails at `B`, and `normalize_checked` at `Unit` returns `NormalForm(x, 2)`: a variable of type $B$ presented as a normal form of type `Unit`. `normalize_eta_long` rejects the term at both types with `TypeMismatch`, because its evaluator checks the arguments in the original context; it is incomplete here but not unsound."
#~ msgstr "具有声明式类型 $B$ 且没有其他类型（外层 $x$ 的类型为 $B$），但 `infer` 在 $\\Gamma, x{:}\\mathsf{Unit}$ 中为第二个参数定型并返回 `Unit`。因此 `check` 在 `Unit` 下成功、在 `B` 下失败，而 `normalize_checked` 在 `Unit` 下返回 `NormalForm(x, 2)`：一个类型为 $B$ 的变量被当作类型为 `Unit` 的范式给出。`normalize_eta_long` 在两个类型下都以 `TypeMismatch` 拒绝该项，因为其求值器在原始上下文中检查参数；它在这里是不完备的，但并非不可靠。"

#~ msgid "[!WARNING] This is a soundness bug of `infer` and `check`, recorded in the correctness checklist and not yet fixed. Renaming the parameter apart from the free variables of $a_2, \\dots, a_n$ before extending the context, or typing $a_2, \\dots, a_n$ in $\\Gamma$ itself, would restore the theorem without its proviso."
#~ msgstr "[!WARNING] 这是 `infer` 和 `check` 的一个可靠性缺陷，已记录在正确性检查清单中，尚未修复。在扩展上下文之前将形参重命名，使其与 $a_2, \\dots, a_n$ 的自由变量相区别，或者直接在 $\\Gamma$ 中为 $a_2, \\dots, a_n$ 定型，都可以恢复该定理而无需其前提。"

#~ msgid "`check` and `infer` terminate; on success, the term is declaratively typable at the reported type, *provided* no redex parameter occurs free in a later argument of its spine. Otherwise `check` can accept a wrong type (known issue above), and so can `normalize_checked`."
#~ msgstr "`check` 与 `infer` 必然终止；成功时，该项在所报告的类型下是声明式可定型的，*前提是*没有可约式的形参在其脊的后续参数中自由出现。否则 `check` 可能接受错误的类型（见上文的已知问题），`normalize_checked` 也是如此。"

#~ msgid "The $\\textsc{Redex}$ rule does not rename its parameter apart from later arguments, so `check` is unsound on redexes whose parameter occurs free in a later argument (known issue)."
#~ msgstr "$\\textsc{Redex}$ 规则不会把其形参重命名以区别于后续参数，因此对于形参在后续参数中自由出现的可约式，`check` 是不可靠的（已知问题）。"

#~ msgid "An empty application `Apply(h, [])` is not a beta redex and hides any redex in its head position (see the [eval design](../eval.md)); build applications with `application` or with at least one argument."
#~ msgstr "空应用 `Apply(h, [])` 不是 β 可约式，并且会隐藏其头部位置中的任何可约式（见 [eval 设计](../eval.md)）；请用 `application` 或至少带一个参数来构建应用。"

#~ msgid "[!WARNING] `@stlc.check` can accept a term at a wrong type when a lambda applied to several arguments has a parameter that occurs free in a later argument. The [stlc API](api/stlc.md) describes the case and how to avoid it."
#~ msgstr "[!WARNING] 当一个应用于多个参数的 lambda 的形参在后面某个实参中自由出现时，`@stlc.check` 可能以错误的类型接受项。[stlc API](api/stlc.md) 描述了这种情形及其规避方法。"

#~ msgid "Known issue: `@stlc.infer` and `@stlc.check` type the later arguments of a redex $(\\lambda x.\\,b)\\,a_1\\,a_2 \\cdots$ with $x$ in scope, so they can accept a wrong type when $x$ occurs free in $a_2, \\dots$ ([stlc design](design/stlc.md))."
#~ msgstr "已知问题：`@stlc.infer` 和 `@stlc.check` 在 $x$ 处于作用域内的情况下为可约式 $(\\lambda x.\\,b)\\,a_1\\,a_2 \\cdots$ 的后续参数定型，因此当 $x$ 在 $a_2, \\dots$ 中自由出现时，它们可能接受错误的类型（[stlc 设计](design/stlc.md)）。"

#~ msgid "**Parameter names in redexes with several arguments.** In $(\\lambda x.\\,b)\\,a_1\\,a_2$, if $a_2$ mentions a free variable also called $x$, `infer` types it with the parameter's type (known issue), and `check` may then accept the term at a type it does not have. Use a parameter name that does not occur free in the later arguments."
#~ msgstr "**多参数可约式中的参数名。** 在 $(\\lambda x.\\,b)\\,a_1\\,a_2$ 中，如果 $a_2$ 提及一个同样叫 $x$ 的自由变量，`infer` 会用参数的类型为它定型（已知问题），于是 `check` 可能以该项实际并不具有的类型接受它。请使用不在后续参数中自由出现的参数名。"

#~ msgid "Import it in `moon.pkg`:"
#~ msgstr "在 `moon.pkg` 中导入它："

#~ msgid "The examples below also use `moonbitlang/core/immut/hashset` for name sets. The mathematics behind these definitions is in the [core design](../design/core.md)."
#~ msgstr "下面的示例还使用 `moonbitlang/core/immut/hashset` 表示名字集合。这些定义背后的数学见 [core 设计](../design/core.md)。"

#~ msgid "It has the step-count contract of `@rewrite.normalize`: at most `max_steps` steps, and one extra `reduce_once` call to classify the final term."
#~ msgstr "它遵循 `@rewrite.normalize` 的步数契约：最多 `max_steps` 步，并额外调用一次 `reduce_once` 来判定最终项。"

#~ msgid "Every element of `steps` is a `Reduced` value; consecutive steps chain, the `after` of one being the `before` of the next. `steps().length()` equals the `steps` count of `result`. `steps()` returns a copy."
#~ msgstr "`steps` 中的每个元素都是一个 `Reduced` 值；相邻步骤首尾相接，前一步的 `after` 即后一步的 `before`。`steps().length()` 等于 `result` 中的 `steps` 计数。`steps()` 返回一个副本。"

#~ msgid "Each test is a hash-set lookup, so the expected cost is $O(|U|)$ lookups in the worst case and one lookup when the hint is already fresh."
#~ msgstr "每次测试是一次哈希集合查找，因此最坏情况下的期望代价是 $O(|U|)$ 次查找，而当提示名本身已是新鲜的时只需一次查找。"

#~ msgid "In a `ReductionTrace`, `steps[0].before = initial`, `steps[i].after = steps[i+1].before`, and the final term of `result` is the last `after` (or `initial` when there are no steps)."
#~ msgstr "在 `ReductionTrace` 中，`steps[0].before = initial`，`steps[i].after = steps[i+1].before`，且 `result` 的最终项是最后一个 `after`（若没有步骤则为 `initial`）。"

#~ msgid "has declarative type $B$ (the outer $x$ has type $B$), but `infer` types the second argument in $\\Gamma, x{:}\\mathsf{Unit}$ and returns `Unit`. `normalize_eta_long` then rejects the term at either type, because its evaluator checks the arguments in the original context. This is a known issue of the current implementation (recorded in the correctness checklist); renaming the parameter apart from the free variables of the remaining arguments avoids it."
#~ msgstr "具有声明式类型 $B$（外层 $x$ 的类型为 $B$），但 `infer` 在 $\\Gamma, x{:}\\mathsf{Unit}$ 中为第二个参数定型并返回 `Unit`。随后 `normalize_eta_long` 在任一类型下都拒绝该项，因为其求值器在原始上下文中检查参数。这是当前实现的一个已知问题（记录在正确性检查清单中）；将形参重命名，使其与其余参数的自由变量相区别，即可避免该问题。"

#~ msgid "The checker terminates: every recursive call is on a strictly smaller term ($\\textsc{Redex}$ recurses on $b\\,a_2 \\cdots a_n$, which is smaller than the redex)."
#~ msgstr "检查器必然终止：每次递归调用都作用于严格更小的项（$\\textsc{Redex}$ 递归处理 $b\\,a_2 \\cdots a_n$，它比该 redex 更小）。"

#~ msgid "`check` and `infer` terminate; on success, the term is declaratively typable at the reported type, subject to the side condition of $\\textsc{Redex}$ (see the known issue above)."
#~ msgstr "`check` 与 `infer` 必然终止；成功时，该项在所报告的类型下是声明式可类型化的，但须满足 $\\textsc{Redex}$ 的附加条件（见上文的已知问题）。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "By induction on $t$. The variable, value and application cases are immediate. For $\\beta x.\\,t$ without renaming, let $\\sigma' = \\sigma \\setminus x$ and assume $x \\n"
#~ "otin R_{\\sigma'}(\\mathrm{FV}(t))$:"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "对 $t$ 归纳。变量、值和应用情形是直接的。对于不需重命名的 $\\beta x.\\,t$，令 $\\sigma' = \\sigma \\setminus x$，并假设 $x \\n"
#~ "otin R_{\\sigma'}(\\mathrm{FV}(t))$："

#~ msgid ""
#~ "Step $(*)$: for $z = x$, $\\sigma'(x) = x$ contributes $\\{x\\}$, which is removed. For $z \\n"
#~ "e x$, $\\sigma'(z) = \\sigma(z)$, and $x \\n"
#~ "otin \\mathrm{FV}(\\sigma(z))$: either $z \\in \\operatorname{dom}\\sigma'$ and $\\mathrm{FV}(\\sigma(z)) \\subseteq R_{\\sigma'}(\\mathrm{FV}(t)) \\n"
#~ "ot\\n"
#~ "i x$, or $\\sigma(z) = z \\n"
#~ "e x$. With renaming, the same computation applies to $x'$ and $t\\{x \\mapsto x'\\}$, where $x' \\n"
#~ "otin \\operatorname{supp}\\sigma'$ makes the side condition hold. $\\square$"
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "步骤 $(*)$：对 $z = x$，$\\sigma'(x) = x$ 贡献 $\\{x\\}$，而它被移除了。对 $z \\n"
#~ "e x$，$\\sigma'(z) = \\sigma(z)$，且 $x \\n"
#~ "otin \\mathrm{FV}(\\sigma(z))$：要么 $z \\in \\operatorname{dom}\\sigma'$ 且 $\\mathrm{FV}(\\sigma(z)) \\subseteq R_{\\sigma'}(\\mathrm{FV}(t)) \\n"
#~ "ot\\n"
#~ "i x$，要么 $\\sigma(z) = z \\n"
#~ "e x$。有重命名时，同样的计算适用于 $x'$ 和 $t\\{x \\mapsto x'\\}$，其中 $x' \\n"
#~ "otin \\operatorname{supp}\\sigma'$ 保证了附加条件成立。$\\square$"

#~ msgid "The variable case is the definition. In the binder case, the renaming test already restricts to $R_{\\sigma'}(\\mathrm{FV}(t))$, so both sides rename the same binders, and only the variables in $\\mathrm{FV}(t) \\setminus \\{x\\}$ are looked up. The fresh names may differ, because they avoid the support of different substitutions, hence equality up to $=_\\alpha$."
#~ msgstr "变量情形即定义本身。在绑定子情形，重命名测试已经限制在 $R_{\\sigma'}(\\mathrm{FV}(t))$ 上，因此两边重命名的是相同的绑定子，并且只查找 $\\mathrm{FV}(t) \\setminus \\{x\\}$ 中的变量。新鲜名字可能不同，因为它们避开的是不同代换的支撑，所以相等只在 $=_\\alpha$ 意义下成立。"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "It suffices to check one alpha step $\\beta x.\\,t =_\\alpha \\beta y.\\,t\\{x \\mapsto y\\}$ with $y \\n"
#~ "otin \\mathrm{names}(t)$. Both sides become binders over the same body up to the bound name, and by Lemma 1 their bodies have the same free variables outside the binder, so they are alpha-equivalent. As a consequence substitution is well defined on alpha-equivalence classes, and the choice of fresh names never matters semantically."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "只需检查一步 α 变换 $\\beta x.\\,t =_\\alpha \\beta y.\\,t\\{x \\mapsto y\\}$，其中 $y \\n"
#~ "otin \\mathrm{names}(t)$。两边都成为在同一个体（至多相差约束名）上的绑定子，并由引理 1，它们的体在绑定子之外具有相同的自由变量，因此它们 α-等价。由此，代换在 α-等价类上是良定义的，新鲜名字的选择在语义上无关紧要。"

#~ msgid "By Lemma 3 we may choose a representative of $t$ in which no binder lies in $\\operatorname{supp}\\sigma \\cup \\operatorname{supp}\\tau$; then no binder is renamed on either side and both substitutions pass under binders unchanged. The variable case splits as in the definition of $\\sigma \\mathbin{;} \\tau$:"
#~ msgstr "由引理 3，可以选取 $t$ 的一个代表元，使其中没有绑定子落在 $\\operatorname{supp}\\sigma \\cup \\operatorname{supp}\\tau$ 中；这样两边都不会重命名任何绑定子，两个代换都原样穿过绑定子。变量情形按 $\\sigma \\mathbin{;} \\tau$ 的定义分情况："

#~ msgid "The application and value cases follow by induction. $\\square$"
#~ msgstr "应用和值的情形由归纳得出。$\\square$"

#~ msgid ""
#~ "For a renaming $\\rho$ and a list of names $L \\supseteq \\mathrm{FV}(t)$, `from_renaming(L, ρ)` is $\\sigma_\\rho = \\{x \\mapsto \\rho(x) \\mid x \\in L,\\ \\rho(x) \\n"
#~ "e x\\}$ (as variables), and $t\\sigma_\\rho =_\\alpha t\\rho$: both replace each free $x$ by the variable $\\rho(x)$, and both freshen a binder exactly when it would capture."
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "对重命名 $\\rho$ 和名字列表 $L \\supseteq \\mathrm{FV}(t)$，`from_renaming(L, ρ)` 为 $\\sigma_\\rho = \\{x \\mapsto \\rho(x) \\mid x \\in L,\\ \\rho(x) \\n"
#~ "e x\\}$（作为变量），且 $t\\sigma_\\rho =_\\alpha t\\rho$：两者都把每个自由的 $x$ 替换为变量 $\\rho(x)$，并且都恰好在会发生捕获时为绑定子取新鲜名字。"

#~ msgid "The algorithm runs in time linear in the size of the terms, plus the cost of the environment lookups (linear in the binder depth)."
#~ msgstr "该算法的运行时间与项的大小成线性，另加环境查找的开销（与绑定深度成线性）。"

#~ msgid "Cost: `free_variables` and `all_names` are linear in the term size (in hash-set operations). `rename_free` and `alpha_rename_bound` are linear when no binder is renamed; each freshened binder adds a traversal of its body."
#~ msgstr "开销：`free_variables` 和 `all_names` 与项的大小成线性（以哈希集合操作计）。当没有绑定子被重命名时，`rename_free` 和 `alpha_rename_bound` 是线性的；每个取新鲜名字的绑定子会额外增加一次对其体的遍历。"

#~ msgid "The substitution lemma (Barendregt 2.1.16, derived in the substitution design) is what makes beta well defined on alpha classes and compatible with contexts."
#~ msgstr "代换引理（Barendregt 2.1.16，在 substitution 设计中推导）使 β 在 α 等价类上良定义，并与上下文相容。"

#~ msgid "**Determinism in the budget.** The computation does not inspect the fuel except to stop, so a run with fuel $f$ that ends with a normal form after consuming $c \\le f$ units performs exactly the same computation with any fuel $f' \\ge c$. Results are therefore reproducible, and `consumed` is the exact minimum budget for that result."
#~ msgstr "**预算中的确定性。** 计算除了用于停止之外不检查燃料，因此一次燃料为 $f$、在消耗 $c \\le f$ 单位后以范式结束的运行，在任意燃料 $f' \\ge c$ 下执行完全相同的计算。因此结果是可复现的，且 `consumed` 恰好是得到该结果所需的最小预算。"

